  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q37-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $P(x)=x^4+3x^3+2x^2+x+1$ and $Q(x)=x^2+2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q37-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $Q(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-5x+1$",
          "worked": "By polynomial division,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nP(x)-x^2Q(x)&=3x^3+x+1\\\\\nP(x)-x^2Q(x)-3xQ(x)&=-5x+1\\\\\nP(x)&=(x^2+2)(x^2+3x)+(-5x+1).\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince the remainder has degree less than 2, the remainder is $-5x+1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q37-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find a polynomial that is divisible by $Q(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^4+3x^3+2x^2+6x$\n\nSubtract the remainder from $P(x)$.",
          "worked": "Subtract the remainder:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nP(x)-(-5x+1)&=x^4+3x^3+2x^2+x+1+5x-1\\\\\nP(x)-(-5x+1)&=x^4+3x^3+2x^2+6x\\\\\nP(x)-(-5x+1)&=(x^2+2)(x^2+3x).\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x^4+3x^3+2x^2+6x$ is divisible by $Q(x)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
